<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/11th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Tamarón</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1037">1037</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Tamarón was fought on 4 September 1037 near Tamarón, west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgos">Burgos</a>, between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bermudo-iii-of-leon">Bermudo III of León</a> and his brother-in-law Ferdinand, count of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a>, aided by his brother García Sánchez III of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-navarre">Navarre</a>. Bermudo was killed, ending the old Asturian-Leonese male line, and Ferdinand took the throne of León by right of his wife Sancha, becoming Ferdinand I.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-tamaron.jpg" alt="Battle of Tamarón" width="320" height="442" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ferdinand_I_of_Le%C3%B3n_cely.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In 1037 Ferdinand I defeated and killed Bermudo III of León at the <b>Battle of Tamarón</b> and was crowned king of León, and he is traditionally counted as the first king of Castile.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-castile">Kingdom of Castile · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>…effectively autonomous in the mid-tenth century, and in 1037 Ferdinand I, count of Castile and son of Sancho III of Navarre, killed Bermudo III, the last king of the old Leonese line, at the <b>Battle of Tamarón</b> and took the Leonese throne by right of his wife Sancha.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-leon">Kingdom of León · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li></ul></section>
